WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.421
Welcome to the SurveyCraft
Specialist certification.

00:00:03.421 --> 00:00:06.118
This course is about designing, building,

00:00:06.118 --> 00:00:10.525
fielding and reporting your own
surveys for clients in SurveyCraft,

00:00:10.525 --> 00:00:13.288
and protecting the people who answer them.

00:00:13.288 --> 00:00:16.248
This orientation takes
about fifteen minutes.

00:00:16.733 --> 00:00:21.074
When you run a Culture Mosaic, a
lot of the quality is built in.

00:00:21.074 --> 00:00:24.127
The items are tested,
the report is designed,

00:00:24.127 --> 00:00:27.450
and the benchmark tells
you what good looks like.

00:00:27.450 --> 00:00:29.689
A custom survey has none of that.

00:00:29.689 --> 00:00:31.384
Its quality is your work.

00:00:31.384 --> 00:00:33.758
That means the questions you write.

00:00:33.758 --> 00:00:38.574
A leading question gets you a flattering
answer that nobody can act on.

00:00:38.574 --> 00:00:40.813
It means the settings you choose.

00:00:40.813 --> 00:00:45.221
If an invitation says "anonymous"
and the settings say otherwise,

00:00:45.221 --> 00:00:48.816
you've broken a promise to
every person who answered.

00:00:48.816 --> 00:00:52.072
And it means how you read
and share the results.

00:00:52.072 --> 00:00:57.634
Four managers in a table are four named
people, whatever the survey called itself.

00:00:57.634 --> 00:01:00.754
This course gives you
the craft for all three.

00:01:00.754 --> 00:01:06.384
You'll plan surveys from the client's
decision, build them properly in SurveyCraft,

00:01:06.384 --> 00:01:09.640
test them, field them,
and report them honestly.

00:01:09.640 --> 00:01:12.217
At the end, you'll build one yourself.

00:01:12.733 --> 00:01:15.677
There are seven modules, taken in order.

00:01:15.677 --> 00:01:19.798
Module 1 covers where surveys
live and who can see them.

00:01:19.798 --> 00:01:21.196
Module 2 is design.

00:01:21.196 --> 00:01:22.741
Module 3 is building.

00:01:22.741 --> 00:01:25.832
Module 4 is settings, privacy and testing.

00:01:25.832 --> 00:01:28.408
Module 5 is fielding and reporting.

00:01:28.408 --> 00:01:31.057
And Module 6 is your practical task.

00:01:31.057 --> 00:01:36.870
Allow about four hours, plus two or three
hours to build your practical survey.

00:01:37.367 --> 00:01:40.417
You're certified when
you clear three gates.

00:01:40.417 --> 00:01:44.437
First, pass each module check
with eighty percent or more,

00:01:44.437 --> 00:01:48.596
and finish the Module 4 simulation
without a critical error.

00:01:48.596 --> 00:01:52.616
A critical error is a choice
that would hurt a respondent.

00:01:52.616 --> 00:01:54.141
Retakes are unlimited.

00:01:54.141 --> 00:01:57.815
Second, the final exam:
thirty questions, open notes.

00:01:57.815 --> 00:02:01.628
You need eighty percent, and
every critical item right.

00:02:01.628 --> 00:02:07.450
Those items cover the things you must never
get wrong, like protecting small groups.

00:02:07.450 --> 00:02:08.906
Third, the practical.

00:02:08.906 --> 00:02:13.134
You'll build and test a short
pulse survey to a client brief,

00:02:13.134 --> 00:02:17.501
and send one file with your
one-page rationale and screenshots.

00:02:17.501 --> 00:02:17.709
Dr.

00:02:17.709 --> 00:02:19.581
Chris Cancialosi scores it.

00:02:20.067 --> 00:02:23.890
Pass all three and you're
Certified, SurveyCraft Specialist.

00:02:23.890 --> 00:02:27.969
It stands on its own, so you don't
need the Mosaic course first.

00:02:27.969 --> 00:02:32.749
With both, you can run the Mosaic tools
and design your own surveys for the

00:02:32.749 --> 00:02:34.470
questions they don't cover.

00:02:34.470 --> 00:02:38.740
The certification lasts five years,
and if you're a Mosaic partner,

00:02:38.740 --> 00:02:43.838
you'll also get the SurveyCraft Specialist
badge on your partner portal profile.

00:02:44.333 --> 00:02:49.306
Wherever you see "Try it", repeat the
step in the Mosaic Practice Workspace.

00:02:49.306 --> 00:02:51.792
You'll build your practical there too.

00:02:51.792 --> 00:02:53.166
Three things to know.

00:02:53.166 --> 00:02:57.877
Every learner shares it and sees your
surveys, so use made-up data only,

00:02:57.877 --> 00:03:02.327
and name each survey with the course
code, your name and what it is.

00:03:02.327 --> 00:03:05.925
It never sends email, so open
surveys from their links.

00:03:05.925 --> 00:03:08.739
And it's wiped on the
first of every month,

00:03:08.739 --> 00:03:11.814
so submit your practical
before the month ends.

00:03:12.300 --> 00:03:17.322
If you took the Mosaic course, you
know Northwind Health: one hospital,

00:03:17.322 --> 00:03:22.486
six clinics, six hundred and forty
people, still settling after a merger.

00:03:22.486 --> 00:03:26.094
Their Culture Mosaic in
February put Collaboration,

00:03:26.094 --> 00:03:28.923
Change Ready and Empowered Teams lowest,

00:03:28.923 --> 00:03:33.026
and their action plan started
cross-site huddles in April.

00:03:33.026 --> 00:03:35.997
Now Alex Moreau, the Chief People Officer,

00:03:35.997 --> 00:03:39.534
wants a quick read before
the board meets in July.

00:03:39.534 --> 00:03:44.273
Are people going to the huddles,
do they help, and if not, why not?

00:03:44.273 --> 00:03:49.295
Riley Okonkwo, their People Analytics
Lead, has drafted some questions.

00:03:49.295 --> 00:03:54.035
You'll take that pulse from draft
to results across Modules 2 to 5.

00:03:54.035 --> 00:03:58.067
Then, in Module 6, you'll
build a second one on your own.

00:03:58.567 --> 00:04:02.046
Before you start, read
the Survey Practice Code.

00:04:02.046 --> 00:04:03.713
It's eight commitments.

00:04:03.713 --> 00:04:09.584
The ones that matter most: promise only
the confidentiality the settings deliver.

00:04:09.584 --> 00:04:13.644
Protect small groups, in every
table, filter and export.

00:04:13.644 --> 00:04:15.456
Ask only what you'll use.

00:04:15.456 --> 00:04:17.630
Keep test data out of results.

00:04:17.630 --> 00:04:22.922
Don't invite a client into a workspace
that holds other clients' surveys.

00:04:22.922 --> 00:04:25.386
Claim only what the data supports.

00:04:25.386 --> 00:04:27.923
Use bought instruments as designed.

00:04:27.923 --> 00:04:31.403
And close the loop with
the people who answered.

00:04:31.900 --> 00:04:34.969
Tick the box to confirm
you'll follow the Code.

00:04:34.969 --> 00:04:39.998
Then, if you like, note one survey you've
seen that promised to be completely

00:04:39.998 --> 00:04:40.651
anonymous.

00:04:40.651 --> 00:04:42.871
We'll come back to it in Module 4.

